<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9848" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιγρᾰφ-ή</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a reply in writing,</i>
			such as Caesar's <u>Anticato</u> in reply to Cicero's
				<i>Cato,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				3
			</span></i>,cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Sol.</u>
				1
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.1059b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herm.
				<u>in Phdr.</u>
				p.189A.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as law-term, <i>answer
				put in by the defendant, plea,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				45.46
			</span></i> (where a specimen is found); sts. of <i>the plaintiff's
				plea, indictment,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				27c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Eux.</u>
				31
			</span></i>:—sts. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιγραφή</span>
			was used indifferently of both parties, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>:—in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				471
			</span></i>, generally, <i>counter-pleas,</i> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				8.58
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>transcribing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				4.62
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίγραφον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.577e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>rescript, imperial decree</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				262.27
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>